From: Ziwei Wu <wuziwei518@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] net: airoha: support hardware flowtable offload for bridge slave ports

In OpenWrt and common router environments, LAN interfaces (such as lan1-lan4
and wireless AP interfaces) are aggregated under a virtual bridge device
(e.g., br-lan).

When the Netfilter flowtable attempts to offload routed traffic destined for
a LAN host, the egress net_device presented to the hardware driver is the
bridge master device (br-lan). Previously, airoha_ppe_foe_entry_prepare()
validated the egress net_device via airoha_is_valid_gdm_dev(). Because the
virtual bridge device is not a physical GDM device, the driver unconditionally
rejected the hardware flow entry with -EINVAL.

As a consequence, routed downlink traffic from WAN to LAN could never be
hardware-offloaded into the PPE flow table, causing up to 88% of incoming
traffic to fall back onto the CPU DMA path (CDM2 and heavy softirq load),
leading to sustained high CPU load under multi-connection workloads like BitTorrent.

Fix this by resolving the bridge slave port via br_fdb_find_port() using the
destination MAC address when netdev is a bridge master (netif_is_bridge_master).
If a corresponding bridge slave port (such as lan1 or phy0-ap0) is found in
the FDB, substitute netdev with the real slave net_device prior to DSA port
and GDM device validation. If the destination MAC is not yet in the FDB,
the flow safely falls back to CPU software routing until the bridge learns it.

Signed-off-by: Ziwei Wu <wuziwei518@gmail.com>
---
--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_ppe.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_ppe.c
@@ -4,6 +4,9 @@
  * Author: Lorenzo Bianconi <lorenzo@kernel.org>
  */
 
+#if IS_ENABLED(CONFIG_BRIDGE)
+#include <linux/if_bridge.h>
+#endif
 #include <linux/airoha-eth.h>
 #include <linux/ip.h>
 #include <linux/ipv6.h>
@@ -462,11 +465,26 @@ static int airoha_ppe_foe_entry_prepare(struct airoha_eth *eth,
 					struct airoha_gdm_dev **egress_dev)
 {
 	u32 qdata = FIELD_PREP(AIROHA_FOE_SHAPER_ID, 0x7f), ports_pad, val;
-	u32 pon_tag = 0;
-	int wlan_etype = -EINVAL, dsa_port = airoha_get_dsa_port(&netdev);
 	struct airoha_foe_mac_info_common *l2;
+	int wlan_etype = -EINVAL, dsa_port;
+	u32 pon_tag = 0;
 	u8 smac_id = 0xf;
 
+#if IS_ENABLED(CONFIG_BRIDGE)
+	if (netdev && netif_is_bridge_master(netdev)) {
+		struct net_device *slave_dev;
+		u16 vid = data->vlan.num ? data->vlan.hdr[data->vlan.num - 1].id : 0;
+
+		slave_dev = br_fdb_find_port(netdev, data->eth.h_dest, vid);
+		if (!slave_dev && vid)
+			slave_dev = br_fdb_find_port(netdev, data->eth.h_dest, 0);
+
+		if (slave_dev)
+			netdev = slave_dev;
+	}
+#endif
+
+	dsa_port = airoha_get_dsa_port(&netdev);
 	memset(hwe, 0, sizeof(*hwe));
 	*egress_dev = NULL;
 
